#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Fail-closed evaluator for FC-01 v1.3 Amendment B.

The normal command evaluates the immutable four-commit activation sequence.
It is deliberately offline: it reads Git objects and local evidence only and
never calls a provider, database, browser, GitHub, or production service.

Auxiliary commands:

* ``--self-test`` runs deterministic in-memory fixture checks.
* ``--print-contracts`` prints the exact seal, activation, projection, clock,
  and approval-validation contracts enforced by this file.
* ``--validate-approval PACKET RECEIPT [CONSUMPTION]`` validates a D1/D2/D3
  packet and its later user-authored receipt (and, when supplied, the one-use
  consumption receipt) against ``approval-schema.json``.
* ``--validate-clock-ledger LEDGER`` validates the 24-active-hour clock while
  independently enforcing the non-pauseable fourteen-day seal expiry.
* ``--validate-ci-lane GATE LANE INPUT`` validates one immutable typed CI
  input envelope using the exact evaluator bytes sealed by Amendment B.

Only the exact projection commit can produce repair authority.  A payload or
seal alone, or even a valid activation receipt without its projections, keeps
all authority flags false.
"""

